# SABOTAGE: the obsolescence write-down loses its ADR-040 Gate — an estimate can
# be posted without a second party's consent.
#
# WS-ACCT Phase 9 (ADR-054 D10) makes `:post` a gated transition: the unwrapped
# call is refused with ApprovalRequired and opens a pending approval; a DISTINCT
# approver's decision re-invokes the action as the requester. This patch deletes
# that one `change({Samen.Approvals.Gate, ...})` line, on the plausible reasoning
# that "the cascade already re-derives the assessment, so a human review adds
# nothing."
#
# Why that reasoning is wrong: the cascade proves the NUMBER is current, not that
# a human agreed to expense it. NRV is an estimate; the whole point of D10 is
# that an estimate never enters the GL on the machinery's own authority. Remove
# the Gate and every other guarantee still holds — the drift check re-derives the
# cents, the entry balances, the lines are append-only, a re-post is refused —
# which is exactly why the arithmetic tests stay green and only the approval test
# reds. A ledger that is arithmetically perfect and unauthorized is the failure.
#
# APP: samen_core
# TEST_FILES: test/finance_reserve_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: the Gate refuses an ungated write-down and a distinct approver lands it once
--- a/samen_core/lib/samen/scopes/finance/reserve_blueprint.ex
+++ b/samen_core/lib/samen/scopes/finance/reserve_blueprint.ex
@@ -282,7 +282,6 @@
 
             validate(Samen.Scopes.Finance.ReserveDraftStatus)
 
-            change({Samen.Approvals.Gate, kind: unquote(Atom.to_string(module)) <> ":post"})
 
             # The outer arm: the posted-born entry's own PostGuard restores the
             # marker BEFORE EntryLines inserts its rows, so the action that
